The export has 427 rows, but 15 report IDs repeat because pages overlap. Counting each ID once leaves 412 unique reports, all merged into #4471.

## Split by cause

| Cause | Reports | Evidence |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `parser` | 379 | The shared parser reads month first, while all 11 affected tenants use day-first dates. These reports came through app, email, and forms. |
| `hint` | 33 | All reports came through booking-v3 forms in three day-first tenants. The field says `MM/DD/YYYY`, then the form reads dates in the tenant's day-first order. |

These need separate tickets: the first is in the shared parser; the second is the booking-v3 field hint and interpretation mismatch. Classify by the tenant's locale and form version in `causeOf`, not the reporter's browser locale or intake tag.

The five reports the desk noted as one-day moves belong to `parser`. The counts use unique report IDs: 379 + 33 = 412.

## Engineering update · 5 October 2026

The desk closed #4471. Engineering fixed the parser with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint was marked **won't fix** because the booking-v3 form was retired.

## Tickets filed

- [**Shared date parser flips day-first dates**](https://github.com/slawomir-t-alle/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) — 379 reports; closed as fixed.
- [**Booking-v3 date hint is month-first for day-first tenants**](https://github.com/slawomir-t-alle/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) — 33 reports; closed as won't fix.

